\title{fairGATE: Fair Gated Algorithm for Targeted Equity}
\description{
fairGATE corrects an independently fitted prediction model for fairness
across protected groups. A cross-fitted base learner (XGBoost or a neural
network, \code{\link[=fairgate_base_learner]{fairgate_base_learner()}}) is fitted without the protected
attribute; a gated mixture of neural experts (\code{\link[=train_gnn]{train_gnn()}}) then learns a
per-person correction to its score under a fairness penalty, for binary or
continuous outcomes and two or more groups. \code{\link[=fairgate]{fairgate()}} runs the whole
method, including the configuration search and selection rule of the
accompanying study, in one call, and \code{\link[=fairgate_export]{fairgate_export()}} returns the
per-person adjustments with their stability intervals.
}
\details{
The neural-network components use the 'torch' package, which needs the
LibTorch backend (\code{torch::install_torch()}). For reproducible fits call
\code{torch::torch_set_num_threads(1)} first.
}
